# Managed by Ansible (roles/setup/claude_code) — edits here are overwritten.
# claude-land@.service refuses an agent PR that changes, adds, deletes or renames out of a path
# under any prefix below, unless the operator approved its head. Plain prefixes, so
# `scripts/deploy_tools/land` covers land.sh, land.py and land_lib/. The modules the landing
# process imports are refused the same way, derived at landing time (land_lib/policy.py,
# gate_hits), so this list holds only what no import walk can see.
#
# DECIDED: a floor, not every path that widens the agent's authority (operator decision,
# 2026-10-10). It keeps the explicit grant points and the gate itself. The agent's roles, the
# deployer and the inventory land without approval. This is not a barrier to root: the deployer
# applies any setup-role change as root, so a task in an unlisted role reaches root. That was
# already true under the wider list. docs/claude-agent-user.md, "The approval floor", has the
# reasoning. The list is literal here, not a variable, so the inventory cannot override it.
#
# The lander: this list, the unit that reads it, the rule that lets the agent start it, and the
# task file that installs them with the lander's settings pinned.
ansible/roles/setup/claude_code/tasks/lander.yml
ansible/roles/setup/claude_code/templates/claude-land-approval-paths.j2
ansible/roles/setup/claude_code/templates/claude-land@.service.j2
ansible/roles/setup/claude_code/templates/50-claude-land.rules.j2
# The landing policy and the code that runs it.
scripts/deploy_tools/land
# The interpreter and packages `uv run` syncs before land.py starts. A package can run code at
# interpreter start through a .pth file, before any policy check.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
uv.toml
.python-version
# CI, which decides what "green" means for the merge.
.github/
# sudo, ssh and the operator's own login.
ansible/roles/setup/initial_setup/tasks/access.yml
# The secrets and who can decrypt them.
ansible/.sops.yaml
ansible/vars/secrets.yml
